    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0101" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/7608</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">24 October, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Thank you for sending me
                    Mr. Phillips’ memorandum about the question put by Mr. de Laboulaye.<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d43-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I think that it would be a mistake for the British and French Governments to
                    address the Japanese Government with the request that Japan should send troops
                    to the West Front next spring and summer, but, of course, I do not wish to press
                    the objection and think it would be unwise to raise one.</p>
                <p>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
